    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d634">

                <pb facs="0774" n="682" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg682"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/9618</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of the Chief of the Division of Latin
                        American Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stabler</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 11, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Guatemalan Minister called to see Mr. Stabler this afternoon and spoke with
                    him in regard to a letter which he had received from the President of Guatemala
                    in which it was stated that serious consideration was being given to the matter
                    of declaration of war against Germany on the part of Guatemala, and he further
                    stated that the matter of expropriation of German property was also being <pb
                        facs="0775" n="683" xml:id="pg683"/> given attention. The Minister stated
                    that he was also advised that further instructions were being sent him by the
                    Guatemalan Foreign Office in regard to German property in Guatemala and, as soon
                    as he received them, he would inform the Department.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d634-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>The Minister further informed Mr. Stabler that he was informed that the
                    Guatemalan Assembly had passed a law authorizing the Government to contract for
                    an amount up to $30,000,000. He informed Mr. Stabler that, as soon as further
                    details were received, he wished to discuss the matter with the Department
                    looking toward some arrangements for a loan in the United States.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stabler</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d634-f1" n="1" xml:id="d634-f1-content">
                <p>For later correspondence regarding German property in Guatemala, see <ref
                        target="frus1918Supp02#pg_366">Supplement 2, pp. 366</ref>–<ref
                        target="frus1918Supp02#pg_373">373</ref>.</p>
            </note>
